==English==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|es}} {{term|calabaza|lang=es||[[pumpkin]], gourd}}, possibly from {{etyl|ar}} {{term|قرعة يابسة|sc=Arab|tr=qárʕa yābisa||dry gourd}} or directly from Persian {{term|خربزه|tr=kharbozeh||melon|lang=fa}}, or from a pre-Roman Iberian word *''calapaccia''; cognate with French {{term|calebasse|lang=fr||gourd}}

===Noun===
{{wikipedia}}
{{en-noun|es}}

# A [[vine]] grown for its [[fruit]], which can either be harvested young and used as a vegetable or harvested mature, dried and used as a container, like a [[gourd]].
# {{originally}} That fruit
# A utensil traditionally made of the dried [[shell]] of a calabash and used as a bottle, dipper, utensil or pipe, etc.
